Classification Catalogues (bound via _data/icd_modules.py):

This repository does NOT contain a copy of the ICD classifications. The
catalogues are bound as external modules at runtime. Their data and licences
belong to their respective owners:

  ICD-10 (WHO, 2019 release)
    Bound via:  simple-icd-10 (PyPI)
    Data:       Public domain (CC0)
    Mode:       Offline
    Upstream:   https://icd.who.int/browse10/

  ICD-10-CM (US clinical modification)
    Bound via:  simple-icd-10-cm (PyPI, MIT-licensed wrapper)
    Data:       Public-domain US federal data (CDC/NCHS)
    Mode:       Offline
    Upstream:   https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/icd/icd-10-cm/
    Caveat:     The packaged release lags the current CDC/NCHS fiscal-year
                release. For billing-relevant coding, verify against the
                current official release.

  ICD-11 (WHO)
    Bound via:  simple-icd-11 (PyPI) against the official WHO ICD-API
    Data:       CC BY-ND 3.0 IGO (World Health Organization)
    Mode:       ONLINE ONLY. Requires free OAuth2 credentials
                (WHO_ICD_CLIENT_ID / WHO_ICD_CLIENT_SECRET), obtainable at
                https://icd.who.int/icdapi
    Behaviour:  Without credentials the ICD-11 binding reports itself as
                unavailable and the application falls back to the bundled
                psychiatric seed catalogue. It does NOT guess codes.

WHO ICD-11 content is licensed CC BY-ND 3.0 IGO. The no-derivatives clause
means WHO ICD-11 content retrieved through the API must not be modified or
redistributed in altered form. This project therefore queries the API at
runtime rather than vendoring or transforming the catalogue.

DSM-5 / DSM-5-TR:

DSM-5 and DSM-5-TR criteria, diagnostic texts, and category names are the
copyright of the American Psychiatric Association and are NOT reproduced in
this repository. Where the software refers to DSM-aligned categories it uses
the ICD-10-CM codes listed in DSM-5-TR, which are public domain, together with
descriptions written for this project.
